{# The progression's séquences, above the one being placed. Creating a progression from several
   séquences lands on the first one's placement, and before this rail the others could only be
   reached by going back through 5a - so a teacher who had just planned four séquences saw one.

   One entry per séquence, in the progression's own order, each carrying the same
   « Placée / Partiellement placée / Non placée » tone as 5a's chip, here as a dot: the rail is a
   way through, not a status table. Its entries are links because moving means a new page - the
   options, the séances and the two actions of this screen are all scoped to one séquence.

   Not rendered for a single séquence - a rail with one entry navigates nowhere. #}
{% if sequences|length > 1 %}
    <nav class="cm-rail" aria-label="{{ 'progressionPlacementSequenceRailLabel'|trans }}">
        <span class="cm-rail__label">{{ 'progressionPlacementSequenceRailLabel'|trans }}</span>
        {% for item in sequences %}
            {% set current = item.id == sequence.id %}
            <a class="cm-rail__item{{ current ? ' is-active' }}"
               href="{{ path('app_progression_placement', {id: progression.id, sequenceId: item.id}) }}"
               title="{{ item.status.labelKey|trans }}"
               {% if current %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                <span class="cm-rail__index">{{ loop.index }}</span>
                <span class="cm-rail__title">{{ item.title }}</span>
                <span class="cm-rail__dot cm-rail__dot--{{ item.status.tone }}"></span>
            </a>
        {% endfor %}
    </nav>
{% endif %}
